WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
Hi I'm Michelle from Lab Muffin Beauty
Science! Today we're going to be talking

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:09.330
about collagen supplements. If you're into
beauty and skin care you may have

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.500
seen collagen supplements around. And
you'll have seen claims like how taking

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.380
collagen will smooth wrinkles, boost
firmness and make your skin more elastic.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:24.960
But do they really work? Since I have a
PhD in medicinal chemistry I needed to

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.750
check out the evidence for myself. Here's
what I found.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.879
Collagen is a protein which means it's
long chain of amino acids chemically

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.390
joined together.
Collagen is an incredibly important

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:47.100
protein that's part of what's called the
extracellular matrix. This holds the

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.770
cells in your body together. It's also
found in bones, tendons and tissue. In

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:57.539
your skin, collagen lives in the lower
layer called the dermis. It's important

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:01.500
for giving your skin structure and
elasticity, which translates to bouncy

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:08.310
skin. As you get older your body produces
less collagen. It's estimated that skin

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:13.229
collagen drops by about 1% per year.
There's also a change in the types of

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:17.970
collagen in your skin so you end up with
thin wrinkly skin that's more prone to

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:23.280
damage. Damage from the environment can
also destroy collagen. Sun exposure and

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.540
smoking are especially harmful.
That's why sun-damaged skin looks older

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:34.020
and sunscreen is so important.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.430
So logically eating collagen could
give your body the building blocks to

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:44.500
make more collagen. Unfortunately you
have very little control over what your

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:50.260
body does with the things you eat. Eating
plants doesn't mean we end up green and

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:56.050
able to photosynthesize and make food
from sunshine. Eating a mirrorball won't

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.580
make you glittery no matter how much you
want to shine.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:06.160
Like I mentioned,
collagen is a protein made up of lots of

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.570
amino acids joined together. In your
stomach and small intestine you have

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:15.040
enzymes that will break up proteins like
collagen into smaller fragments so you

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.540
can absorb them into your body. So most
of the time when you eat a protein it

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.840
will get broken up and your body won't
be able to tell which protein you've

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:29.290
eaten. But collagen has a special amino
acid in it: hydroxyproline. In humans

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:34.750
hydroxyproline is only found in collagen.
So when you eat collagen you'll end up

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.120
with hydroxyproline in your blood, so
your body can tell you've eaten collagen.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.620
But does this do anything?

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:51.439
There have been a bunch of studies where
collagen supplements improve skin in

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:56.810
mice and rats and even pigs. It's also
been found that after eating a collagen

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:00.709
supplement human volunteers have
fragments of broken-down collagen called

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:07.670
prolyl-hydroxyproline in their blood. In
vitro, prolyl-hydroxyproline fragments were

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.170
found to make human skin cells grow
faster and produce more hyaluronic acid,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:17.689
another component of the dermis.
Hyaluronic acid keeps the water content

00:03:17.689 --> 00:03:23.180
in your skin high which is also
important for bouncy unwrinkled skin. But

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:26.750
the study doesn't tell us anything about
whether the fragments get from the blood

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:30.709
to the skin in high enough
concentrations to actually do anything,

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.569
which is sort of absolutely crucial to
whether or not collagen supplements work.

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:40.519
So does it work in actual people?
Here's what the clinical trials have

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:45.889
found so far. In one study by a
supplement company volunteers took 5

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:50.419
grams of hydrolyzed collagen made from
fish cartilage every day along with

00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:56.479
other vitamins and minerals. After 60
days, dryness, wrinkles and the depth of

00:03:56.479 --> 00:03:59.900
the nasolabial fold
(that's the groove between your nose and

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:06.139
cheek) improved, and after 12 weeks
collagen density and skin firmness also

00:04:06.139 --> 00:04:11.780
improved. But most parts of the trial
didn't use a placebo control so it isn't

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:18.199
as reliable, and of course there's the
bias issue. In another study volunteers

00:04:18.199 --> 00:04:21.620
took either a daily supplement
containing 2.5 grams of

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.960
collagen peptide or a placebo for eight
weeks. There were improvements in eye

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.729
wrinkles as well as procollagen and
elastin content of the dermis. The trial

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:36.320
was run independently by a university.
The same supplement also improved skin

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.550
elasticity four weeks after the
volunteers stopped taking the supplement.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.440
10 grams of a daily collagen peptide
supplement was found to improve skin

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.460
hydration after eight weeks, and
increased density and decreased

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.719
fragmentation of collagen in the dermis
after four weeks, according to placebo

00:04:53.719 --> 00:04:57.909
controlled trials run by the manufacturer.

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:05.979
So right now you're probably thinking
that we should all immediately run out

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:10.599
and eat all of the collagen supplements.
But before you spend all your money I

00:05:10.599 --> 00:05:15.669
have to burst your bubble a little bit
with some inconvenient facts. One of the

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:19.569
big issues with supplement studies is
that they often use supplements that

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:24.129
contain ingredients other than collagen
as well, so you can't say for sure that

00:05:24.129 --> 00:05:28.449
it's collagen having the effect and not
the other ingredients. For the non

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:32.440
placebo controlled trials it could also
be something else entirely causing the

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:37.690
change. For collagen it's particularly
tricky because there are at least 28

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:43.719
types of collagen. Collagen is also made
up of thousands of amino acids. Most

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:48.219
studies use collagen that's been
hydrolyzed or broken up, but as you can

00:05:48.219 --> 00:05:52.419
imagine with a chain that's thousands of
amino acids long, you can break it up

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:56.919
into different lengths. So a supplement
with collagen that's a thousand amino

00:05:56.919 --> 00:06:01.449
acids long might not have the same
effect as one that uses fragments that

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:07.599
are 100 amino acids long or 50 amino
acids long or 10 amino acids long. So

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:11.589
even if a study finds a beneficial
effect with one collagen supplement it

00:06:11.589 --> 00:06:16.330
doesn't mean that a different collagen
supplement will also work. If that's not

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.770
enough another issue is that a lot of
these studies are done by companies who

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.389
sell the supplements so there's an
obvious conflict of interest. It's

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:29.740
unlikely that they'll publish data that
show that there isn't any effect, and

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.690
it's likely that they have massaged the
results to look as good as possible.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:39.310
Here's the verdict: collagen supplements
are pretty promising and could

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:44.889
potentially work, but the evidence is far
from solid. Only a few collagen

00:06:44.889 --> 00:06:48.729
supplements have gotten good results in
studies and collagen supplements can be

00:06:48.729 --> 00:06:53.680
very different. And most of these studies
were run by the companies that sell the

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:58.449
collagen supplements, so they're likely
to be biased. The results also don't

00:06:58.449 --> 00:07:03.159
really find that collagen supplements
actually increase collagen and not just

00:07:03.159 --> 00:07:07.689
improve your skin through other methods
like increasing hyaluronic acid,

00:07:07.689 --> 00:07:12.879
or just indirectly changing your diet.
For example if you drink more collagen

00:07:12.879 --> 00:07:16.959
based supplements maybe it makes you eat
less sugar because you're full from the

00:07:16.959 --> 00:07:22.089
water, and it's actually the lower sugar
that improves your skin. If you have the

00:07:22.089 --> 00:07:26.289
budget there isn't much harm in trying
collagen supplements as long as you

00:07:26.289 --> 00:07:30.249
don't have an allergy, but if you want
the best bang for your buck I'd

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:34.839
recommend trying more proven ways of
protecting and increasing your collagen

00:07:34.839 --> 00:07:37.110
first.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:45.030
Preventing collagen from being destroyed
in the first place is much easier and

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:49.620
more effective than trying to repair
your skin later, so make sure you wear a

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:54.960
high UVA protection sunscreen daily. One
study found that collagen gets damaged

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.260
with about one-tenth of the UV that
causes a sunburn,

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:04.500
so not burning doesn't mean your skin
isn't being damaged. Vitamin C is also

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:08.700
great as an antioxidant for soaking up
free radicals that cause sun damage and

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:14.580
it can also increase collagen as well.
Vitamin A derivatives known as retinoids

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.480
are the gold standard for increasing
collagen in your skin, particularly

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:23.460
tretinoin. Glycolic acid has been found
to increase collagen in some studies as

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:29.250
well. If you want to get more hardcore,
chemical peels can increase collagen. So

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:35.460
can laser and IPL light treatments. If
you want to go super basic you should

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:40.410
make sure that your skin is adequately
hydrated. Dehydrated skin is a really

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:45.330
common cause of tired looking skin and
it's very easy to fix. Look for serums

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.510
and moisturizers with humectant
ingredients that help your skin hold

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:54.260
onto water, like glycerin and hyaluronic
acid to plump up skin and hide wrinkles.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.590
That's all from me about collagen
supplements. I'm sure there'll be more

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:02.250
research soon on collagen that tells
us more about whether or not it actually

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:07.380
works. If you like my video I'd love it
if you could subscribe to my channel! You

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.310
can also follow me on Instagram and
Facebook for more beauty-based science tips (oops)

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:16.590
You can also check out my blog for tons
and tons of beauty science. See you next

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.740
time!

